# HAL wiring for the panic controller safety MCU component.
# Add these lines to your machine's HAL config file.
#
# The component:
#   - reads OK/PANIC from the ESP32 over USB CDC (/dev/ttyACM0)
#   - drives estop-ok LOW on any fault or lost connection
#   - sends ESTOP to the ESP32 when LinuxCNC enters estop
#   - auto-resets LinuxCNC estop when the physical ack button is pressed
#     (operator only needs to press cycle start to resume)

# Load the component — -Wn specifies the HAL component name to wait for
loadusr -Wn panic-controller python3 /home/conor/linuxcnc/configs/myCoolMachine/panic_controller.py

# Drive LinuxCNC's external estop input from the controller state.
# When estop-ok is LOW, LinuxCNC stays in estop regardless of F1.
unlinkp iocontrol.0.emc-enable-in
net safety-estop  panic-controller.estop-ok  =>  iocontrol.0.emc-enable-in
